INT. CAPSIZED SAILBOAT - UPSIDE-DOWN CABIN - NIGHT

Hull turned to ceiling. Black water at knee height, sloshing. A galley stove hangs overhead like a bat. One headlamp.

LAKSHMI VENKAT (30s, navigator, orange float coat) clings to a bunk rail. Water to her ribs. Breath fogging.

OTIS BRANNIGAN (50s, skipper, split eyebrow) wedges himself against the companionway, shoulder to the hatch.

Third: HENRIK SOLBERG (20s, deckhand, teeth chattering) pulls himself up on a pipe cot.

OTIS
Count off.

LAKSHMI
One.

HENRIK
Two.

OTIS
Three. Good. Air?

LAKSHMI
We've got maybe an hour.

HENRIK
Less. I can taste it.

Otis slams the hatch with his shoulder. Water spits through the seams. Lakshmi swings the headlamp to the porthole, where something white and heavy bobs against the glass, and Henrik grabs a boat hook off the wall and jabs at the hatch latch while Otis hauls himself up the ladder, and the whole hull rolls another few degrees, tipping a gush of black over all three of them.

LAKSHMI
It's moving!

OTIS
Hold on!

HENRIK
(overlapping)
We're going down!

LAKSHMI
(overlapping)
We're not going down, we're settling!

OTIS
Both of you, quiet!

They go quiet. The hull ticks. Somewhere far above, faint through steel: an engine.

HENRIK
Is that...

OTIS
Shh.

LAKSHMI
It's a ship.

OTIS
Bang the hull. Everyone.

They bang the hull with fists, with the boat hook, with a skillet from the galley. Three rhythms, three desperate voices. The engine slows. Stops.

Silence. Then, from above: three knocks.
